 "notes": "Series lists turned into issuer-series archetypes with versions from retrieved Wikipedia pages; series without a retrieved page stay in m (Argentina, Israel, Korea, Thailand, Philippines, New Zealand, South Africa, Dominion of Canada, HM Treasury). Pick numbers not added: no catalogue page retrieved. 'Obsolete banknote' renamed Private and local bank note; US Treasury issues (United States Notes, silver and gold certificates, Treasury Coin Notes, Educational Series) moved from it to Circulation banknote as the United States Treasury notes archetype because they are federal issues, not bank notes. Japanese occupation (Philippines) and Hawaii overprint notes moved from emergency scrip to Military and occupation currency. Facsimile/counterfeit and prop/souvenir kinds merged into Replica, prop or counterfeit note. Error note is new, sourced to the Notaphily article; no individually named error notes found."
